WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:08.320
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, this is going
to be all about the end of the Star Wars Universe.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:12.360
At Dark Horse Comics.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:18.820
After December 31st they are not allowed to
print or sell any new copies of any of their

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:19.820
Star Wars comics.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:20.820
I’ve also got some Episode 7 news, but holy
shit.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:21.820
No more Dark Horse Star Wars.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:25.230
In honor of that Dark Horse is doing this
epic Farewell Digital Bundle.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:29.670
You can buy every single Star Wars title they
ever printed for $300.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.629
It’s not a going out of business sale or
anything.

00:00:32.629 --> 00:00:35.739
As some of you correctly assumed.

00:00:35.739 --> 00:00:47.039
Because Disney owns Star Wars and they took
the rights to the comics.

00:00:47.039 --> 00:00:49.350
Dark Horse isn’t making new ones.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:53.109
I flipped a little when I found out that the
Disney deal goes beyond that.

00:00:53.109 --> 00:00:57.359
Dark Horse has to stop selling new versions
of their old comics.

00:00:57.359 --> 00:01:00.649
In case you don’t read a lot of comics,
it’s just like new printings of old books.

00:01:00.649 --> 00:01:05.111
The Lord of the Rings books were originally
published in the 1950s and every couple of

00:01:05.111 --> 00:01:06.970
years a new edition is released.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:10.550
If you’re old enough or a big comics historian
you might remember the original Marvel Star

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:11.550
Wars comics.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.000
After New Hope was released in theaters in
1977, Lucasfilm granted the comic book rights

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.000
to Marvel.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.990
It started as a direct adaptation of the movies
but then they branched the stories out.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:20.560
It ran for 107 issues till 1986.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:26.220
They had a letters to the editor column in
it called “Star Words”.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.630
That was like right before Jim Shooter came
in.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:31.970
Marvel went through like 3 editor-in-chiefs
at the time.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:35.020
Supposedly some of the people that worked
there at the time say that their big franchise

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:36.730
deal with Star Wars saved Marvel from bankruptcy,
because Star Wars was so popular.

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:42.000
1986, the year Marvel printed their last Star
Wars comic, was also the same year Dark Horse

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.370
Comics was founded as a company.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.650
They didn’t start publishing Star Wars comics
till 1991.

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:45.910
But Dark Empire was their first storyline.

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:49.530
It was probably the first time I ever thought
about a specific comic book that I really

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:50.530
wanted.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:56.500
I was just a little kid and I think one of
my friends got Issue Number 1 and it was the

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.560
most amazing thing I’d ever seen.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:01.290
It was right before they re-released the original
trilogy in THX, that was 1995 and the Star

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:03.180
Wars Insider Fan Club became a thing in 1994.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.880
So for most children of the 80s, the Dark
Horse comics were you’re only way to experience

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:06.890
new stories set in the Star Wars universe.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:08.869
The funny thing is that now it’s more than
20 years later.

00:02:08.869 --> 00:02:34.120
The majority of us who were little kids then,
probably have little kids ourselves who are

00:02:34.120 --> 00:03:25.530
going to learn about Star Wars from all the
new Disney Marvel stuff.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:50.489
Dark Empire and Tales of the Jedi were my
favorite storylines from all the Dark Horse

00:03:50.489 --> 00:03:51.489
stuff.

00:03:51.489 --> 00:03:54.970
But just for fun my TOP 5 titles from worst
to best are

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:59.790
Their First Boba Fett Solo Title, The Mara
Jade Solo Title, Fall of the Sith Empire,

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:02.050
Golden Age of The Sith and Dark Empire.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:03.050
Just the first Dark Empire.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.870
I didn’t like Dark Empire 2 as much.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:08.700
You can kind of tell I stopped reading the
Dark Horse stuff after I got too busy with

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:09.700
school.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:14.700
So all of the stuff they published after the
prequels I have not read.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:17.090
Let me know what you’re favorite Star Wars
comic is.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:21.959
And even if you don’t want to buy the $300
special deal you can still buy individual

00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:23.419
comics at a 50 percent discount.

00:04:23.419 --> 00:04:26.710
I think most of them are half off.

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:30.139
It’s all on Dark Horse’s website.

00:04:30.139 --> 00:04:39.990
So 
now that we’ve shed a tear for our childhood

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:40.990
let’s talk about Episode 7.

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:41.990
I’m still totally calling it Episode 7.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:42.990
It just seems more natural.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:51.139
The newest rumor is that one of the Spinoffs
will be a Suicide Squad team up style movie

00:04:51.139 --> 00:04:56.550
about the team that stole the plans for the
original death star.

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:59.819
It would involve Han Solo’s character, Aaron
Paul and Max Von Sydow are supposedly involved

00:04:59.819 --> 00:05:02.229
and it would tie in with Episode 8.

00:05:02.229 --> 00:05:04.669
The one Rian Johnson is working on.

00:05:04.669 --> 00:05:08.400
The movie itself would be a grittier heist
type movie set before the events of Episode

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:09.400
4.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:14.090
Remember, the plans were stolen, then Vader
chased down Princess Leia because he knew

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:17.080
she was connected with the Rebellion and might
have the plans.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:21.520
Which she stashed in R2.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:41.229
That way they’d still be able to use the
character and Harrison Ford would have to

00:05:41.229 --> 00:05:55.939
be in 
every single movie.

00:05:55.939 --> 00:06:02.240
Here’s a big question.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:18.080
Do you want to see one of the new spinoff
movies take place before or in and around

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:24.240
the original trilogy?

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:28.370
We had the Prequels, but I think the idea
with these new films is to create a very diverse

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:30.159
looking star wars movie universe.

00:06:30.159 --> 00:06:37.650
They’ve been picking directors and writers
that are all known for very different types

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:42.020
of movies.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.020
All of them good.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:47.900
I’m super excited about Episode 7, but really
I’m a much bigger fan of Rian Johnson.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:58.069
So Episode 8 I think will be much 
more interesting.

00:06:58.069 --> 00:07:09.939
And just as a point of reference, Marvel is
doing the same thing with it’s films too.

00:07:09.939 --> 00:07:17.620
It’s got so many, they’re essentially
giving really good indie filmmakers a chance

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:22.009
to make a big studio film and bring their
creativity to it, and because they’re indie

00:07:22.009 --> 00:07:23.009
directors.

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:26.949
They don’t have to pay them Michael Bay,
JJ Abrams level salaries.

00:07:26.949 --> 00:07:35.139
There’s also something to be said about
not letting JJ Abrams or the other super-producers

00:07:35.139 --> 00:07:39.060
out there have total control over the look
and feel of every major franchise.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.639
Even Joss Whedon is stepping back a bit after
Age of Ultron.

00:07:41.639 --> 00:07:46.729
He’ll still be a producer on Marvel films,
but mostly he’ll be in a support role.

00:07:46.729 --> 00:07:51.030
Helping them fix story problems and making
sure it all hits the level of quality Marvel

00:07:51.030 --> 00:08:37.630
wants 

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:56.660
to hit.

